{"causes": ["The ongoing struggle for ecclesiastical independence of the Polish church from German archdioceses, especially Magdeburg, necessitated strong leadership.", "The political fragmentation of Poland after Bolesław III Wrymouth's testament created an urgent need for institutional stability within the church.", "The desire of the Piast dynasty to strengthen its sovereignty through an independent national church provided political backing for Jakub's efforts."], "effects": ["The Gniezno Bull of 1136 secured the jurisdictional independence of the Gniezno Archdiocese from foreign ecclesiastical claims.", "Jakub's efforts provided a detailed legal and geographical record of early 12th-century Poland through the comprehensive enumeration in the Gniezno Bull.", "The strengthened position of the Gniezno metropolitanate contributed to the consolidation of Polish national identity and statehood in the medieval period."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "innocent-ii", "sourceName": "Pope Innocent II", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "targetName": "Jakub of Żnin", "context": "Pope Innocent II issued the papal bull *Ex commisso nobis* (Gniezno Bull) in 1136, affirming the rights advocated by Jakub of Żnin."}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "gniezno-archdiocese", "targetName": "Gniezno Archdiocese", "context": "Jakub of Żnin significantly influenced the Gniezno Archdiocese by securing its independence and defining its territorial rights through the Gniezno Bull in 1136."}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "gniezno-poland", "targetName": "Gniezno, Poland", "context": "Jakub of Żnin served as the Archbishop of Gniezno, the ecclesiastical capital of Poland, from c. 1124 until 1148."}, {"sourceSlug": "gniezno-bull-1136", "sourceName": "Gniezno Bull (1136)", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "targetName": "Jakub of Żnin", "context": "The Gniezno Bull of 1136 is a defining document of Jakub of Żnin's archiepiscopal tenure, embodying his successful diplomatic efforts."}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "synod-of-łęczyca-1136", "targetName": "Synod of Łęczyca (1136)", "context": "Jakub of Żnin presided over the Synod of Łęczyca in 1136, addressing important matters of clerical discipline and church property in Poland."}], "places": [{"name": "Gniezno, Poland", "role": "Archiepiscopal See"}, {"name": "Łęczyca, Poland", "role": "Synod Location"}, {"name": "Rome, Papal States", "role": "Papal Diplomacy Center"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Jakub of Żnin", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "jakub-of-żnin"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3160358", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakub_of_%C5%BBnin"], "tags": ["Poland", "Religious Figures", "Europe", "comparative-religion", "doctrine-development", "cultural-diffusion"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Jakub of Żnin's successful acquisition of the Gniezno Bull in 1136 critically secured the Polish church's independence from German metropolitanates, directly shaping the ecclesiastical and political landscape of medieval Poland. This act fortified Polish sovereignty and provided an invaluable historical record of the 12th-century state.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-08-05T07:23:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30983353196", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Jakub of Żnin was an early archbishop of Gniezno in Poland. He was archbishop from c. 1124 until 1148.", "newValue": "Jakub of Żnin (died 1148) served as the Archbishop of Gniezno, the ecclesiastical capital of Poland, from approximately 1124 until his death. His tenure was pivotal in solidifying the nascent Polish church's administrative and jurisdictional independence amidst ongoing political fragmentation following the death of Bolesław III Wrymouth. He played a crucial role in negotiating the papal bull *Ex commisso nobis* from Innocent II in 1136, a document that definitively affirmed the Gniezno metropolitanate's supremacy over all Polish dioceses and effectively secured the Polish church's autonomy from German ecclesiastical claims, particularly those of Magdeburg.

Elevated to the primatial see during a period of intense internal conflict and external pressure, Jakub focused on institutionalizing the Polish church's structure. He presided over synods, notably the Synod of Łęczyca in 1136, which addressed clerical discipline and property rights. Jakub's most enduring achievement was his successful advocacy before the Holy See, culminating in the issuance of the Gniezno Bull. This charter meticulously listed and confirmed the properties and jurisdictions of the Gniezno Archdiocese, including over 400 place names, thereby providing an invaluable snapshot of early 12th-century Polish geography, demographics, and legal customs.

The Gniezno Bull, secured by Jakub, became a foundational legal instrument for the Polish church and a primary source for understanding the social and economic landscape of early Piast Poland. Its detailed enumeration of properties and people provided a robust legal basis against foreign ecclesiastical encroachment and internal disputes, ensuring the continued viability and independence of the Polish metropolitanate. Jakub's efforts set a precedent for future archbishops to defend the autonomy of the Polish church against both imperial and internal challenges."}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-05T07:23:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30983353196", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1001"}, {"title": "Spiritual seeking and religious community formation", "type": "Idea", "year": "1001"}], "newValue": ["The ongoing struggle for ecclesiastical independence of the Polish church from German archdioceses, especially Magdeburg, necessitated strong leadership.", "The political fragmentation of Poland after Bolesław III Wrymouth's testament created an urgent need for institutional stability within the church.", "The desire of the Piast dynasty to strengthen its sovereignty through an independent national church provided political backing for Jakub's efforts."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-05T07:23:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30983353196", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped religious practice and spiritual communities", "type": "Idea", "year": "1148"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1148"}], "newValue": ["The Gniezno Bull of 1136 secured the jurisdictional independence of the Gniezno Archdiocese from foreign ecclesiastical claims.", "Jakub's efforts provided a detailed legal and geographical record of early 12th-century Poland through the comprehensive enumeration in the Gniezno Bull.", "The strengthened position of the Gniezno metropolitanate contributed to the consolidation of Polish national identity and statehood in the medieval period."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-08-05T07:23:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#30983353196", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "country-poland", "targetName": "Poland", "context": "Jakub of Żnin associated with Poland"}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "PREACHES", "targetSlug": "field-250", "targetName": "Religious Figures", "context": "Jakub of Żnin: Religious teaching in religious figures"}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "medieval", "targetName": "Medieval Era", "context": "Jakub of Żnin was active during the Medieval era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "innocent-ii", "sourceName": "Pope Innocent II", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "targetName": "Jakub of Żnin", "context": "Pope Innocent II issued the papal bull *Ex commisso nobis* (Gniezno Bull) in 1136, affirming the rights advocated by Jakub of Żnin."}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "gniezno-archdiocese", "targetName": "Gniezno Archdiocese", "context": "Jakub of Żnin significantly influenced the Gniezno Archdiocese by securing its independence and defining its territorial rights through the Gniezno Bull in 1136."}, {"sourceSlug": "jakub-of-żnin", "sourceName": "Jakub of Żnin", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "gniezno-poland", "targetName": "Gniezno, Poland", "context": "Jakub of Żnin served as the Archbishop of Gniezno, the ecclesiastical capital of Poland, from c. 1124 until 1148."}, {"sourceSlug": "gniezno-bull-1136", "sourceName": "Gn